\details{
This experimental API is frozen and scheduled for removal in Tempest 0.2.0.
No compatibility shim is planned; see
\link{tempest-generic-kernel-retirement}.

These functions provide host applications with stable access to mutable
\code{TempestRun} state without reaching into R6 fields or methods directly.
Event filtering preserves run-local sequence order. Approval controls remain
nonblocking: automatic resume stops again if another approval is required.

\strong{Host record contracts.}

Run status is one of \code{pending}, \code{running}, \code{awaiting_approval}, \code{succeeded},
\code{failed}, \code{cancel_requested}, \code{cancelled}, or \code{partially_recovered}.

Each event record contains \code{event_id}, a positive run-local \code{sequence},
\code{run_id}, \code{workflow_id}, \code{event_type}, \code{status}, \code{timestamp}, and a
serializable \code{payload}. Context fields \code{step_id}, \code{attempt}, \code{expert_id},
\code{artifact_id}, \code{approval_id}, and \code{message} are \code{NULL} when they do not
apply.

Approval records are named by \code{approval_id} and contain \code{approval_kind}
(\code{step} or \code{artifact}), \code{step_id}, \code{artifact_ids}, \code{status}, \code{reason},
\code{policy_decision_id}, \code{requested_at}, \code{decided_at}, \code{note}, and serializable
\code{metadata}.

Capability grants are named by step id. Each step record contains the
latest \code{attempt}, per-expert \code{experts} grants, step-level \code{step} grants,
\code{recorded_at}, and a named \code{attempts} history. Individual grants contain
capability and operation ids and versions, required and status flags,
connection reference ids, denial reason fields, and serializable metadata.
